    "mechanism": "The hypothesis bet on vision persistence helping at onsets is FALSIFIED by the archive: at steep image-rise onsets the IMAGE forecast is the WORST component (75-100% WAPE) \u2014 worse than direct ctx (57-72%) and far worse than requests (33-38%). The image spike itself is unforecastable at onsets, so the additive route inherits no vision advantage; its tiny 15s edge traces to the well-forecast REQUESTS term, not images.",
    "decision": "CLOSE as NEGATIVE. Do NOT graduate to a planner run. The direct ctx forecast already captures the image-driven component as well as (or better than) a structural decomposition can, because the image component is least forecastable exactly where the edge was expected."
